  "decision_date": "26/10/2012",
  "description": "Reconfiguration and refurbishment of former magistrates court to provide restaurant/cafe at ground/lower ground floors, with creation of nine flats over upper and extended second floor levels. Provision of new ramp access to main entrance and new landscaped area to front.",
  "site_name": "Magistrates Court",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "23/07/2012",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "TW8 8EN",
  "street_name": "Market Place",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "lapsed_date": "26/10/2015",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted  therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted development have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details. \r\nDetails shall include Alterations to stone and brickwork: areas of new-build will require samples to be agreed; brick panel/s to display bricks and mortar should include the\r\nspecification and profile of jointing. Metal and panel work: materials to be agreed, and should include information on joints such as seams and their direction where these are\r\nvisible.",
    "Condition : 4 - No development hsall take place until details, including 1:25 plans, and samples of any proposed fenestration alterations, have been subitted to abnd apoproevd in writing by the LPA. Details shall be implemented as approved.",
    "Condition : 5 - Sustainability - No development shall take place until details have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority, for a scheme meeting the requirements of Policy 5.2 of the London Plan which asks for a 25%\r\nreduction in regulation CO2 emissions below the Part L 2010 TER - through energy efficiency or/and renewables) where feasible. The details shall be carried out as approved.",
    "Condition : 6 - The A3 use hereby permitted shall not be open to customers outside the following times - 9am to 11pm.",
    "Condition : 7 - No deliveries shall be taken at or despatched from the site outside the hours of 9am to 11pm nor at any time on Sundays, Bank or Public Holidays.",
    "Condition : 8 - The external front podium area and forecourt shall not be used in conjunction with the hereby approved A3 use outside the following times 9am-930pm.",
    "Condition : 9 - The use hereby permitted for A3 purpose shall not be begun until full particulars and details of a scheme to insulate the premises against the transmission of airborne and impact sound has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given.",
    "Condition : 10 - The uses hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials in respect of both the residential and commercial units  have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 11 - No development shall take place until details of a salvage and reuse strategy has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\nDetails shall include strategies for the reuse of existing external and internal features which already (or could, with careful repair and refurbishment) add to the character and\r\nappearance of the building. Details should include where possible, existing guard railings\r\nwhere they have good design and detail being be re-used or re-sited nearby; any that are not reused should be salvaged not scrapped. External doors and stair railings of original good design and character that exist should be retained and reused even if relocated;\r\nAreas where brick or stone is changed should have elements such as keystones and rubbed brick arches retained and reused; or at least salvaged not scrapped.",
    "Condition : 12 - Public realm (town square) - Prior to the occupation of any part of the development, full\r\ndetails of the proposed landscaping of the front forecourt of the site will have been\r\nsubmitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\nDetails shall include hard and soft landscaping materials, planting plans and maintenance\r\nschedules as well as proposed finished levels or contours; means of enclosure and the\r\nboundary treatment to demonstrate connectivity with the adjacent public spaces.\r\nThe development shall not be occupied until the details have been implemented as\r\napproved."
  ],
